From 7ae6c4b24d4d83580878dbb3abe00387a4336559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hans Bihs <hans.bihs@reefconsulting.no>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:24:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FNPF 6DOF: X 35, the psi solves start from the extrapolation
 of the last two of their kind

A psi solve of the loads started from the last solution of its kind: psi_0 from the previous
stage, a unit mode from the previous added mass.  With X 35 1 it starts from the linear
extrapolation in time of the last two solutions of the same kind: psi_0 of the same stage of
the previous two steps (the stages of the SSP schemes are not equally spaced in time, the same
stage of consecutive steps is), a unit mode of the previous two added masses, with subcycling
psi_0 of the same stage of the previous two finest steps (fnpf_6DOF_grid::h1, h2 per grid and
kind; psi_guess, psi_record).  The extrapolation factor is limited to 2.  Default 0: as before.

The right-hand side of a psi solve has terms lagged from the initial guess (the explicit sigma
cross-derivatives without A 328 1, the slope part of the bed ghost nodes), so X 35 changes the
results at the level of that lag, not only within the solver tolerance: LUPA float on a
refined 3D mesh, 12 s, Fz within 0.09 % of the amplitude, PTO power 20.0992 -> 20.0996 W;
2D box on a refined mesh, 20 s, motion and loads within 0.06 %; the same box on the uniform
grid, surge amplitude 3 % and My 2 % (the surge force is a small residual there, and the lag
itself is large: A 328 1 or A 324 3 change My by 30 % in that case).

Iterations per psi solve: LUPA 3D 2.77 -> 1.88 (400 steps), 2.89 -> 2.24 (1500 steps); with
X 30 100 as well 1.19 and 1.52; 2D box refined 2.12 -> 1.82, with X 30 100 1.06.

